/**
 *
 * @defgroup geant4 geant4
 *   The code for the Geant4 toolkit.
 *
 *   Geant4's code is organised into a series of _categories_ that contain the
 *   code for specific capabilities.
 *
 *
 * 
 *   @defgroup global global
 *     @ingroup geant4
 *     This is the global category
 *   @defgroup global_management management
 *     @ingroup global
 *     This is the management subcategory of the global category
 *
 *     @todo How to name nested groups (arguments to defgroup)?
 *
 *
 *   @defgroup geometry geometry
 *     @ingroup geant4
 *     Top level category for Geant4's geometry modeling and navigation code.
 *     
 *     More detailed documentation can go here.
 *
 *     @sa global_management
 *
 *     @defgroup geometry_management management
 *       @ingroup geometry
 *       This is the management subcategory of the geometry category
 *
 *     @defgroup geometry_biasing biasing
 *       @ingroup geometry
 *       This is the biasing subcategory of the geometry category
 *
 *     @defgroup geometry_divisions divisions
 *       @ingroup geometry
 *       This is the divisions subcategory of the geometry category
 *
 *     @defgroup geometry_magneticfield magneticfield
 *       @ingroup geometry
 *       This is the magneticfield subcategory of the geometry category
 *
 *     @defgroup geometry_navigation navigation
 *       @ingroup geometry
 *       This is the navigation subcategory of the geometry category
 *
 *     @defgroup geometry_solids solids
 *       @ingroup geometry
 *       This is the solids subcategory of the geometry category
 *
 *       @defgroup geometry_solids_boolean boolean
 *         @ingroup geometry_solids
 *         This is the Boolean subcategory of the geometry_solids category
 *
 *       @defgroup geometry_solids_csg csg
 *         @ingroup geometry_solids
 *         This is the CSG subcategory of the geometry_solids category
 *
 *       @defgroup geometry_solids_specific specific
 *         @ingroup geometry_solids
 *         This is the Specific subcategory of the geometry_solids category
 *
 *     @defgroup geometry_volumes volumes
 *       @ingroup geometry
 *       This is the volumes subcategory of the geometry category
**/
